IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), PART VII.1, sections 152.1 (establishment of the benefit period),
-- 152.11 (its beginning, length, late claims, cancellation, end and extension) and 152.12 (notification).
-- Piece ei5, written by the piece agent ei5 (Sonnet 5.5). Layer 1: from the Act's text alone, no point of view.
--
-- A week is the DATE of its Sunday (keel convention). A judgment the Act hands to the Commission ("shows ... good cause")
-- is a BOOLEAN input named for the showing; this module never decides it. The maxima of s 152.14(1) that s 152.11(14) and
-- (16) rely on are plain inputs (ei5-payment holds s 152.14; this module imports no other ei5 module).
-- Dates: no enactment or commencement date in these sections.

§ `152.1 Establishment of the benefit period`

-- Subsection (1): when a self-employed person who qualifies under s 152.07 makes an initial claim, a benefit period shall be
-- established, and benefits are payable for each week of unemployment that falls in it.
-- src:2403 | 152.1 (1) When a self-employed person who qualifies under section 152.07 makes an initial claim for benefits, a benefit period shall be established and, once it is established, benefits are payable to the person in accordance with this Part for each week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.1(1) (src:2403)
GIVEN `qualifies under section 152.07` IS A BOOLEAN
      `makes an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.1(1) a benefit period shall be established` IF
        `qualifies under section 152.07`
    AND `makes an initial claim for benefits`

-- src:2403 | 152.1 (1) When a self-employed person who qualifies under section 152.07 makes an initial claim for benefits, a benefit period shall be established and, once it is established, benefits are payable to the person in accordance with this Part for each week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.1(1) (src:2403)
GIVEN `a benefit period has been established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is a week of unemployment of the self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: regs 30.1 and 30.2 (piece er2)
      `the week falls in the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.1(1) benefits are payable for the week` IF
        `a benefit period has been established`
    AND `the week is a week of unemployment of the self-employed person`
    AND `the week falls in the benefit period`

-- Subsection (2): no benefit period is established unless (a) the person makes an initial claim in accordance with s 50 and
-- the regulations and proves that they are qualified, and (b) supplies the information the Commission directs.
-- src:2405 | (2) No benefit period is to be established for a self-employed person unless
-- src:2406 | (a) the person makes an initial claim for benefits in accordance with section 50 and the regulations and proves that the person is qualified to receive benefits; and
-- src:2407 | (b) the person supplies information in the form and manner directed by the Commission, giving the person’s employment circumstances and the circumstances pertaining to any interruption of earnings, and any other information that the Commission may require.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.1(2) (src:2405-2407)
GIVEN `the person makes an initial claim for benefits in accordance with section 50 and the regulations and proves that the person is qualified to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 50 (piece ei2)
      `the person supplies information in the form and manner directed by the Commission, giving the person's employment circumstances and the circumstances pertaining to any interruption of earnings, and any other information that the Commission may require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.1(2) the conditions for establishing a benefit period are met` IF
        `the person makes an initial claim for benefits in accordance with section 50 and the regulations and proves that the person is qualified to receive benefits`
    AND `the person supplies information in the form and manner directed by the Commission, giving the person's employment circumstances and the circumstances pertaining to any interruption of earnings, and any other information that the Commission may require`

§ `152.11 The benefit period`

-- Subsection (1): the benefit period begins on the later of (a) the Sunday of the week in which the interruption of earnings
-- occurs and (b) the Sunday of the week in which the initial claim is made (a claim regarded as made earlier under
-- subsection (4) is made on that earlier day).
-- src:2409 | 152.11 (1) A benefit period begins on the later of
-- src:2410 | (a) the Sunday of the week in which the interruption of earnings occurs,
-- src:2411 | and
-- src:2412 | (b) the Sunday of the week in which the initial claim for benefits is made.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(1) (src:2409-2412)
GIVEN `the day on which the interruption of earnings occurs` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the initial claim for benefits is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 152.11(1) the day on which a benefit period begins` IS
    IF `the Sunday of the week of the claim` GREATER THAN `the Sunday of the week of the interruption`
    THEN `the Sunday of the week of the claim`
    ELSE `the Sunday of the week of the interruption`
    WHERE
        `the Sunday of the week of the interruption` MEANS `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day on which the interruption of earnings occurs`
        `the Sunday of the week of the claim` MEANS `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day on which the initial claim for benefits is made`

-- Subsection (2): the length of a benefit period is 52 weeks, except as (11) to (19) provide. The benefit period is the days
-- from the day it begins for that many whole weeks, so it ends on the last day of the last week. The length itself is
-- `s 152.11(2), (15) and (16) the length of the benefit period, in weeks` below.
-- src:2414 | (2) The length of a benefit period is 52 weeks, except as otherwise provided in subsections (11) to (19).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(2) (src:2414)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period begins` IS A DATE
      `the length of the benefit period, in weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 152.11(2) the day on which the benefit period would otherwise end` IS
    `the day on which the benefit period begins` PLUS ((`weeks as days` `the length of the benefit period, in weeks`) MINUS 1)

-- Subsection (3): a benefit period shall not be established if a prior benefit period has not ended (subject to any change
-- or cancellation of a benefit period under this section).
-- src:2416 | (3) Subject to any change or cancellation of a benefit period under this section, a benefit period shall not be established for a self-employed person if a prior benefit period has not ended.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(3) (src:2416)
GIVEN `a prior benefit period has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.11(3) a benefit period may be established despite a prior benefit period` IF
    NOT (`a prior benefit period has not ended`)

-- The three together: qualifies and makes an initial claim, the conditions of (2) are met, and no prior benefit period is open.
-- src:2403 | 152.1 (1) When a self-employed person who qualifies under section 152.07 makes an initial claim for benefits, a benefit period shall be established and, once it is established, benefits are payable to the person in accordance with this Part for each week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period.
-- src:2405 | (2) No benefit period is to be established for a self-employed person unless
-- src:2406 | (a) the person makes an initial claim for benefits in accordance with section 50 and the regulations and proves that the person is qualified to receive benefits; and
-- src:2407 | (b) the person supplies information in the form and manner directed by the Commission, giving the person’s employment circumstances and the circumstances pertaining to any interruption of earnings, and any other information that the Commission may require.
-- src:2416 | (3) Subject to any change or cancellation of a benefit period under this section, a benefit period shall not be established for a self-employed person if a prior benefit period has not ended.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.1(1), (2) and s 152.11(3) (src:2403) (src:2405-2407) (src:2416)
GIVEN `qualifies under section 152.07` IS A BOOLEAN
      `makes an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions of subsection 152.1(2) are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a prior benefit period has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.1 and s 152.11(3) a benefit period is established` IF
        `s 152.1(1) a benefit period shall be established` `qualifies under section 152.07` `makes an initial claim for benefits`
    AND `the conditions of subsection 152.1(2) are met`
    AND `s 152.11(3) a benefit period may be established despite a prior benefit period` `a prior benefit period has not ended`

§§ `152.11(4) to (6.2) Late claims`

-- Subsection (5.1): for subsections (4) and (5), the fact that but for clause 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) (the $5,000 amount of 2021)
-- the claimant would not have qualified is good cause for a delay.
-- src:2422 | (5.1) For the purposes of subsections (4) and (5), the fact that, but for clause 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A), the claimant would not have qualified to receive benefits is good cause for a delay in making a claim for those benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(5.1) (src:2422)
GIVEN `but for clause 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) the claimant would not have qualified to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.11(5.1) that fact is good cause for a delay in making a claim` IF
    `but for clause 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) the claimant would not have qualified to receive benefits`

-- Subsections (6), (6.1) and (6.2): a claim referred to in s 152.06 (152.061, 152.062) shall not be regarded as made on an
-- earlier day under (4) or (5) if (a) when the claim is made all benefits that might have been payable have been exhausted,
-- (b) the beginning of the period in 152.06(3) (152.061(3), 152.062(3)) has been determined and the claim would move it to
-- an earlier date, or (c) the claim is made in other circumstances set out in the regulations (none found).
-- src:2424 | (6) A claim for benefits referred to in section 152.06 with respect to a family member shall not be regarded as having been made on an earlier day under subsection (4) or (5) if
-- src:2425 | (a) at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted;
-- src:2426 | (b) the beginning of the period referred to in subsection 152.06(3) has already been determined with respect to that family member and the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date; or
-- src:2427 | (c) the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations.
-- src:2429 | (6.1) A claim for benefits referred to in section 152.061 with respect to a critically ill child must not be regarded as having been made on an earlier day under subsection (4) or (5) if
-- src:2430 | (a) at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted;
-- src:2431 | (b) the beginning of the period referred to in subsection 152.061(3) has already been determined with respect to that child and the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date; or
-- src:2432 | (c) the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations.
-- src:2434 | (6.2) A claim for benefits referred to in section 152.062 with respect to a critically ill adult must not be regarded as having been made on an earlier day under subsection (4) or (5) if
-- src:2435 | (a) at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted;
-- src:2436 | (b) the beginning of the period referred to in subsection 152.062(3) has already been determined with respect to that adult and the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date; or
-- src:2437 | (c) the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(6), (6.1), (6.2) (src:2424-2427) (src:2429-2432) (src:2434-2437)
GIVEN `at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to the claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beginning of the period has already been determined and the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: ss 152.11(6)(c), (6.1)(c), (6.2)(c); none found
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 152.11(6), (6.1) and (6.2) the claim is not regarded as made on an earlier day` IF
       `at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to the claim have already been exhausted`
    OR `the beginning of the period has already been determined and the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date`
    OR `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`

-- Subsection (4): an initial claim made after the day on which the person first qualified to make it is regarded as made on
-- an earlier day if the person shows that they qualified on the earlier day and that there was good cause for the delay
-- throughout the period from the earlier day to the day the claim was made. The result is the day the claim is regarded as
-- made. "Shows ... good cause" is the Commission's judgment, a BOOLEAN input; (5.1) is one good cause; (6) to (6.2) take the
-- antedating away for the three kinds of caring claim.
-- src:2418 | (4) An initial claim for benefits made after the day on which the self-employed person first qualified to make the claim shall be regarded as having been made on an earlier day if the self-employed person shows that they qualified to receive benefits on the earlier day and that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period that begins on the earlier day and ends on the day on which the initial claim was made.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(4) (src:2418)
GIVEN `the day on which the initial claim was made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person first qualified to make the claim` IS A DATE
      `the earlier day claimed` IS A DATE
      `the person shows that they qualified to receive benefits on the earlier day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day on which the claim was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for clause 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) the claimant would not have qualified to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is not regarded as made on an earlier day under subsection (6), (6.1) or (6.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 152.11(4) the day on which an initial claim for benefits is regarded as having been made` IS
    IF     `the day on which the initial claim was made` GREATER THAN `the day on which the person first qualified to make the claim`
       AND `the earlier day claimed` LESS THAN `the day on which the initial claim was made`
       AND `the person shows that they qualified to receive benefits on the earlier day`
       AND (   `the person shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day on which the claim was made`
            OR `s 152.11(5.1) that fact is good cause for a delay in making a claim` `but for clause 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) the claimant would not have qualified to receive benefits`)
       AND NOT (`the claim is not regarded as made on an earlier day under subsection (6), (6.1) or (6.2)`)
    THEN `the earlier day claimed`
    ELSE `the day on which the initial claim was made`

-- Subsection (5): the same for a claim other than an initial claim, made after the time prescribed for making it (the
-- regulations fix the time; piece er2).
-- src:2420 | (5) A claim for benefits, other than an initial claim for benefits, made after the time prescribed for making the claim shall be regarded as having been made on an earlier day if the self-employed person shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period that begins on the earlier day and ends on the day on which their claim was made.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(5) (src:2420)
GIVEN `the day on which the claim was made` IS A DATE
      `the claim is made after the time prescribed for making the claim` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the Regulations on the time for claims (piece er2)
      `the earlier day claimed` IS A DATE
      `the person shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day on which the claim was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for clause 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) the claimant would not have qualified to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is not regarded as made on an earlier day under subsection (6), (6.1) or (6.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 152.11(5) the day on which a claim other than an initial claim is regarded as having been made` IS
    IF     `the claim is made after the time prescribed for making the claim`
       AND `the earlier day claimed` LESS THAN `the day on which the claim was made`
       AND (   `the person shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day on which the claim was made`
            OR `s 152.11(5.1) that fact is good cause for a delay in making a claim` `but for clause 152.07(1)(d)(i)(A) the claimant would not have qualified to receive benefits`)
       AND NOT (`the claim is not regarded as made on an earlier day under subsection (6), (6.1) or (6.2)`)
    THEN `the earlier day claimed`
    ELSE `the day on which the claim was made`

§§ `152.11(7) to (10) Cancelling and ending the benefit period`

-- Subsection (7)(a): the Commission may cancel a benefit period that has ended if no benefits were paid or payable during it.
-- src:2439 | (7) Once a benefit period has been established for a self-employed person, the Commission may
-- src:2440 | (a) cancel the benefit period if it has ended and no benefits were paid or payable during the period; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(7)(a) (src:2439-2440)
GIVEN `the benefit period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no benefits were paid or payable during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.11(7)(a) the Commission may cancel the benefit period` IF
        `the benefit period has ended`
    AND `no benefits were paid or payable during the period`

-- Subsection (7)(b): whether or not it has ended, at the request of the person, the Commission may cancel the portion
-- immediately before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable, if the person (i) establishes a new benefit
-- period (under this Part or under Part I as an insured person) beginning that first week and (ii) shows good cause for the
-- delay in making the request throughout the period from the day benefits were first paid or payable to the request.
-- src:2439 | (7) Once a benefit period has been established for a self-employed person, the Commission may
-- src:2441 | (b) whether or not the period has ended, cancel at the request of the self-employed person that portion of the benefit period immediately before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable, if the self-employed person
-- src:2442 | (i) establishes under this Part — or establishes under Part 1, as an insured person — a new benefit period beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable, and
-- src:2443 | (ii) shows that there was good cause for the delay in making the request throughout the period that begins on the day on which benefits were first paid or payable and ends on the day on which the request for cancellation was made.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(7)(b) (src:2439) (src:2441-2443)
GIVEN `the person requests the cancellation of the portion of the benefit period immediately before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person establishes a new benefit period beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person shows that there was good cause for the delay in making the request throughout the period from the day benefits were first paid or payable to the day of the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.11(7)(b) the Commission may cancel the portion of the benefit period immediately before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` IF
        `the person requests the cancellation of the portion of the benefit period immediately before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable`
    AND `the person establishes a new benefit period beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable`
    AND `the person shows that there was good cause for the delay in making the request throughout the period from the day benefits were first paid or payable to the day of the request`

-- src:2445 | (8) A cancelled benefit period or portion of a benefit period is deemed never to have begun.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(8) (src:2445)
GIVEN `the benefit period or portion of it has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.11(8) the benefit period or portion of it is treated as having begun` IF
    NOT (`the benefit period or portion of it has been cancelled`)

-- Subsection (9)(c): the person (i) requests that their benefit period end, (ii) makes a new initial claim, and (iii)
-- qualifies under this Part or, as an insured person, under Part I. The paragraph is met on the day the last of the three has
-- happened; NOTHING while any of them has not.
-- src:2450 | (c) the self-employed person
-- src:2451 | (i) requests that their benefit period end,
-- src:2452 | (ii) makes a new initial claim for benefits, and
-- src:2453 | (iii) qualifies to receive benefits under this Part or qualifies, as an insured person, to receive benefits under Part I.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(9)(c) (src:2450-2453)
GIVEN `the day on which the person requests that their benefit period end` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the person makes a new initial claim for benefits` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the person qualifies to receive benefits under this Part or, as an insured person, under Part I` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 152.11(9)(c) the day on which the person has requested the end of the benefit period, made a new initial claim and qualified` IS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the person requests that their benefit period end`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST r THEN
        CONSIDER `the day on which the person makes a new initial claim for benefits`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST c THEN
            CONSIDER `the day on which the person qualifies to receive benefits under this Part or, as an insured person, under Part I`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST q THEN JUST (`the later of` (`the later of` r c) q)

-- Subsection (9): a benefit period ends when the first of three things occurs: (a) no further benefits are payable (including
-- because the maximum weeks of s 152.14 have been paid), (b) it would otherwise end under this section, (c) the request
-- event above. The caller passes the day of (b) (the first day plus its length, less one: see the length rule).
-- src:2447 | (9) A benefit period ends when any of the following first occurs:
-- src:2448 | (a) no further benefits are payable to the self-employed person in their benefit period, including for the reason that benefits have been paid for the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid under section 152.14;
-- src:2449 | (b) the benefit period would otherwise end under this section; or
-- src:2450 | (c) the self-employed person
-- src:2451 | (i) requests that their benefit period end,
-- src:2452 | (ii) makes a new initial claim for benefits, and
-- src:2453 | (iii) qualifies to receive benefits under this Part or qualifies, as an insured person, to receive benefits under Part I.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(9) (src:2447-2453)
GIVEN `the day on which no further benefits are payable to the self-employed person in their benefit period` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the benefit period would otherwise end under this section` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person has requested the end of the benefit period, made a new initial claim and qualified` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 152.11(9) the day on which the benefit period ends` IS
    `the earlier of` `the day on which the benefit period would otherwise end under this section`
        (`the earlier of` `the day under paragraph (a), or the day under paragraph (b) if there is none` `the day under paragraph (c), or the day under paragraph (b) if there is none`)
    WHERE
        `the day under paragraph (a), or the day under paragraph (b) if there is none` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which no further benefits are payable to the self-employed person in their benefit period`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day on which the benefit period would otherwise end under this section`
            WHEN JUST d THEN d
        `the day under paragraph (c), or the day under paragraph (b) if there is none` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the person has requested the end of the benefit period, made a new initial claim and qualified`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day on which the benefit period would otherwise end under this section`
            WHEN JUST d THEN d

-- Subsection (10): a request under (9)(c) is regarded as made on an earlier day if the person shows good cause for the delay
-- throughout the period from the earlier day to the day the request was made, whether or not the benefit period has ended.
-- src:2455 | (10) Whether or not the benefit period has ended, a request under paragraph (9)(c) shall be regarded as having been made on an earlier day if the self-employed person shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period that begins on the earlier day and ends on the day on which the request was made.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(10) (src:2455)
GIVEN `the day on which the request was made` IS A DATE
      `the earlier day claimed` IS A DATE
      `the person shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day on which the request was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 152.11(10) the day on which a request that the benefit period end is regarded as having been made` IS
    IF     `the earlier day claimed` LESS THAN `the day on which the request was made`
       AND `the person shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day on which the request was made`
    THEN `the earlier day claimed`
    ELSE `the day on which the request was made`

§§ `152.11(2) and (11) to (16) Length and extension of the benefit period`

-- Subsection (11): the benefit period is extended by the aggregate of the weeks in it for which the person proves that they were
-- not entitled to benefits because they were (a) confined in a jail, penitentiary or similar institution and not found guilty
-- of the offence they were held for or another offence from the same transaction, (b) in receipt of earnings paid because of
-- the complete severance of their relationship with their former employer, (c) in receipt of workers' compensation payments
-- for an illness or injury, or (d) in receipt of payments under a provincial law on the basis of having ceased to work because
-- continuing to work would have been dangerous to the person, her unborn child or a child she was breast-feeding.
-- src:2457 | (11) A self-employed person’s benefit period is extended by the aggregate of any weeks during the benefit period for which the self-employed person proves, in the manner that the Commission may direct, that they were not entitled to benefits because they were
-- src:2458 | (a) confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution and were not found guilty of the offence for which they were being held or any other offence arising out of the same transaction;
-- src:2459 | (b) in receipt of earnings paid because of the complete severance of their relationship with their former employer;
-- src:2460 | (c) in receipt of workers’ compensation payments for an illness or injury; or
-- src:2461 | (d) in receipt of payments under a provincial law on the basis of having ceased to work because continuing to work would have resulted in danger to the self-employed person, her unborn child or a child whom she was breast-feeding.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(11) (src:2457-2461)
GIVEN `the weeks of the benefit period for which the person proves they were not entitled because confined in a jail, penitentiary or similar institution and not found guilty` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks for which the person proves they were not entitled because in receipt of earnings paid because of the complete severance of their relationship with their former employer` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks for which the person proves they were not entitled because in receipt of workers' compensation payments for an illness or injury` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks for which the person proves they were not entitled because in receipt of payments under a provincial law on the basis of having ceased to work because continuing to work would have been dangerous` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.11(11) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` IS
    `the weeks of the benefit period for which the person proves they were not entitled because confined in a jail, penitentiary or similar institution and not found guilty`
        PLUS `the weeks for which the person proves they were not entitled because in receipt of earnings paid because of the complete severance of their relationship with their former employer`
        PLUS `the weeks for which the person proves they were not entitled because in receipt of workers' compensation payments for an illness or injury`
        PLUS `the weeks for which the person proves they were not entitled because in receipt of payments under a provincial law on the basis of having ceased to work because continuing to work would have been dangerous`

-- Subsection (12): a further extension by the aggregate of the weeks, during an extension under (11), for which the person
-- proves they were not entitled for a reason specified in (11).
-- src:2463 | (12) A self-employed person’s benefit period is extended by the aggregate of any weeks during an extension of a benefit period under subsection (11) for which the self-employed person proves, in the manner that the Commission may direct, that they were not entitled to benefits because of a reason specified in that subsection.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(12) (src:2463)
GIVEN `the weeks during an extension under subsection (11) for which the person proves they were not entitled because of a reason specified in that subsection` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.11(12) the number of weeks of the further extension` IS
    `the weeks during an extension under subsection (11) for which the person proves they were not entitled because of a reason specified in that subsection`

-- Subsection (13): if the child or children referred to in s 152.05(1) are hospitalized during the period in s 152.05(2), the
-- benefit period is extended by the number of weeks of hospitalization.
-- src:2465 | (13) If the child or children referred to in subsection 152.05(1) are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection 152.05(2), the benefit period is extended by the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(13) (src:2465)
GIVEN `the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection 152.05(2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.11(13) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended because the child or children are hospitalized` IS
    `the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection 152.05(2)`

-- Subsection (14): benefits were paid for more than one of the reasons in 152.14(1)(a) to (f), at least one of those benefits
-- was paid for fewer than the applicable maximum number of weeks, and the maximum total number of weeks for those reasons is
-- greater than 50: the benefit period is extended so that those benefits may be paid up to that maximum total. The text does
-- not say by how many weeks (see "what the source does not answer"), so the length rule below takes that number as an input.
-- src:2467 | (14) If, during a self-employed person’s benefit period, benefits were paid to the person for more than one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) to (f), at least one of those benefits was paid for fewer than the applicable maximum number of weeks established for those reasons and the maximum total number of weeks established for those reasons is greater than 50, the benefit period is extended so that those benefits may be paid up to that maximum total number of weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(14) (src:2467)
GIVEN `the number of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) to (f) for which benefits were paid during the benefit period` IS A NUMBER
      `at least one of those benefits was paid for fewer than the applicable maximum number of weeks established for the reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum total number of weeks established for those reasons` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.11(14) the benefit period is extended so that those benefits may be paid up to the maximum total` IF
        `the number of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) to (f) for which benefits were paid during the benefit period` GREATER THAN 1
    AND `at least one of those benefits was paid for fewer than the applicable maximum number of weeks established for the reason`
    AND `the maximum total number of weeks established for those reasons` GREATER THAN 50

-- Subsection (14.1): no benefits were paid for any reason in 152.14(1)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f), and benefits were paid for the
-- reason in (b) where the applicable maximum is the 61 weeks of (b)(ii): extended by 26 weeks.
-- src:2469 | (14.1) If, during a self-employed person’s benefit period, benefits were not paid for any reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f), and benefits were paid to the person for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b) in the case where the applicable maximum number of weeks is established under subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(ii), the benefit period is extended by 26 weeks so that benefits may be paid up to that maximum number of weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(14.1) (src:2469)
GIVEN `benefits were paid for any reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election made` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.11(14.1) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` IS
    IF     NOT (`benefits were paid for any reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f)`)
       AND `benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 152.14(1)(b)`
       AND `the election made` EQUALS `the 61-week maximum`
    THEN 26
    ELSE 0

-- Subsection (16): unless the benefit period is also extended under any of (11) to (13), an extension under (14) must not
-- make the benefit period more than the sum of two weeks and the total of the maximum numbers of weeks established under
-- 152.14(1) for each of the benefits paid for one of the reasons (a) to (f) during the benefit period before the extension.
-- A caller passes one maximum per benefit paid.
-- src:2473 | (16) Subject to subsection (15), unless the benefit period is also extended under any of subsections (11) to (13), an extension under subsection (14) must not result in a benefit period of more than the sum of two weeks and the total of the maximum number of weeks established under subsection 152.14(1) for each of the benefits paid to the self-employed person for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) to (f) during the person’s benefit period before it was extended under subsection (14).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(16) (src:2473)
GIVEN `the maximum numbers of weeks established under subsection 152.14(1) for each of the benefits paid for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) to (f)` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.11(16) the longest a benefit period extended under subsection (14) may be, in weeks` IS
    2 PLUS sum `the maximum numbers of weeks established under subsection 152.14(1) for each of the benefits paid for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) to (f)`

-- Subsection (2), with (11) to (16): the length of a benefit period is 52 weeks except as (11) to (19) provide. The extensions
-- under (11) to (14.1) together must not make it more than 104 weeks (15); and where only (14) extends it, not more than the
-- sum of (16). (17) to (19) are repealed.
-- src:2414 | (2) The length of a benefit period is 52 weeks, except as otherwise provided in subsections (11) to (19).
-- src:2471 | (15) An extension under one or more of subsections (11) to (14.1) must not result in a benefit period of more than 104 weeks.
-- src:2473 | (16) Subject to subsection (15), unless the benefit period is also extended under any of subsections (11) to (13), an extension under subsection (14) must not result in a benefit period of more than the sum of two weeks and the total of the maximum number of weeks established under subsection 152.14(1) for each of the benefits paid to the self-employed person for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 152.14(1)(a) to (f) during the person’s benefit period before it was extended under subsection (14).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.11(2), (15) and (16) (src:2414) (src:2471) (src:2473)
GIVEN `the weeks under subsection (11)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks under subsection (12)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks under subsection (13)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks by which the benefit period is extended under subsection (14), to allow the benefits to be paid up to the maximum total` IS A NUMBER   -- the text does not fix this number
      `the weeks under subsection (14.1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the longest the benefit period may be under subsection (16), in weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.11(2), (15) and (16) the length of the benefit period, in weeks` IS
    IF `only subsection (14) extends the benefit period`
    THEN min (min `the length with all extensions` 104) `the longest the benefit period may be under subsection (16), in weeks`
    ELSE min `the length with all extensions` 104
    WHERE
        `the length with all extensions` MEANS
            52 PLUS `the weeks under subsection (11)` PLUS `the weeks under subsection (12)` PLUS `the weeks under subsection (13)`
               PLUS `the weeks by which the benefit period is extended under subsection (14), to allow the benefits to be paid up to the maximum total`
               PLUS `the weeks under subsection (14.1)`
        `only subsection (14) extends the benefit period` MEANS
                `the weeks by which the benefit period is extended under subsection (14), to allow the benefits to be paid up to the maximum total` GREATER THAN 0
            AND `the weeks under subsection (11)` PLUS `the weeks under subsection (12)` PLUS `the weeks under subsection (13)` EQUALS 0

§ `152.12 Notification`

-- On receiving an initial claim the Commission shall decide whether the self-employed person is qualified and notify the person
-- of its decision: the person is owed the decision and the notice. The decision itself is the Commission's judgment.
-- src:2476 | 152.12 On receiving an initial claim for benefits, the Commission shall decide whether the self-employed person is qualified to receive benefits and notify the person of its decision.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.12 (src:2476)
GIVEN `the Commission has received an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.12 the person is owed a decision on whether they are qualified and notice of the decision` IF
    `the Commission has received an initial claim for benefits`
